<p>Use this dialog box to register custom paper sizes. Up to ten custom 
 paper sizes can be registered. Depending on the printer you are using, 
 up to 100 custom paper sizes can be registered.</p>
<p>The graphic illustrates which dimension is width " A ", and 
 which dimension is length " B " in relation to the feed direction.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="list" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size List:</span></p>
<p>Displays the registered custom paper names and sizes.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Edit</span></p>
<p>Make settings for custom paper sizes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="name" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Name:</span></p>
<p>In <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size List:</span>, select an unused 
 name, and then change it as necessary.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="unit" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Measurement Unit:</span></p>
<p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">inch</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">mm</span> 
 as the units of measurement.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="widthlength" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Width:</span></p>
<p>Enter the size of the paper edge (A) that is vertical relative to the 
 feed direction of the printer.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Length:</span></p>
<p>Enter the size of the paper edge (B) that is horizontal relative to 
 the feed direction of the printer.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="modify" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Modify</span></p>
<p>Click to update the <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size List:</span> 
 with the settings specified here.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
